Enterprise Security Monitoring shall incorporate User and Entity Behavior Analytics (UEBA) to identify abnormal behavior that may indicate security threats.

UEBA shall analyze

- user authentication behavior
- privileged account activity
- workload behavior
- service account activity
- API consumption patterns
- device behavior
- application behavior
- data access patterns
- network communications
- administrative actions

Behavioral baselines shall be continuously updated.

Anomalies shall contribute to Enterprise risk scoring and threat detection.

