# 25. Enterprise Security Monitoring Anti-Patterns

The following architectural anti-patterns are prohibited.

## Isolated Monitoring

Security monitoring shall not be implemented as isolated, application-specific solutions without Enterprise integration.

---

## Incomplete Telemetry

Critical Enterprise assets shall never operate without appropriate security telemetry.

---

## Excessive Alert Noise

Alert rules shall be continuously tuned to minimize false positives and analyst fatigue.

---

## Unprotected Logs

Security logs shall never be stored without integrity protection, access control and appropriate retention.

---

## Manual Correlation

Manual correlation shall not replace automated Enterprise correlation capabilities except during exceptional investigations.

---

## Missing Governance

Security monitoring implementations shall never operate outside Enterprise governance, documentation and audit requirements.

